ObservationUI optional model integrations

This directory contains wrappers, adapters and helper processes for optional
model components. The directory name and the application's edition tiers do
not impose a blanket non-commercial licence on every file or dependency.

Integration source
Project-authored integration source follows the repository's first-party
licence scope and any applicable file-specific or third-party exceptions.
This notice does not grant or change rights in that source. Preserve existing
third-party copyright, licence and attribution notices.

Fetched software
Cellpose and Trackastra code are declared BSD-3-Clause; micro-sam code is
declared MIT. Their separately installed dependencies have their own terms.
Trackastra's locked environment includes Gurobi (proprietary); the current
adapter calls greedy_nodiv linking. That execution choice does not change
Gurobi's installation or licence terms. Exact package versions, hashes and
model sources are recorded in services/uv.lock and the applicable entries
and environment locks under catalog/models/.

Weights and data
Model weights, fine-tuned weights and training or input data have separate
rights from the software that processes them. The catalog records micro-sam's
vit_b_lm weights as CC-BY-4.0 and records non-commercial training-data terms
for several training sets used by micro-sam and Cellpose-SAM. The retained
Trackastra general_2d declaration does not establish its training-data terms.
A user-added Cellpose model has its maker's weight terms, recorded on its
catalog entry. These declarations and the application's policy tiers do not
determine the legal effect of training data on weights or clear a particular
use. Fine-tuning does not itself clear the source weights or training inputs.

Edition policy
The current component registry assigns Cellpose-SAM, its fine-tuned and
user-added variants, micro-sam-lm, Trackastra and Gurobi to the noncommercial
tier. The research edition permits all registered tiers. The commercial
edition permits only open and terms tiers. MICROMIND_EDITION unset or empty
defaults to research; an invalid nonempty value uses the commercial gate.
These are application availability rules, not a licence grant or a finding
that a component is legally suitable for a use.

See services/orchestrator/licences.py, docs/licences.md, this directory's
README.md and the applicable catalog entries and installed-package notices.
